# Keep the function bundle to the server and its dependencies.
#
# Not `functions.excludeFiles` in vercel.json: that key only accepts patterns
# under `api/`, and a root-level entrypoint (see `[tool.vercel]` in
# pyproject.toml) fails the build with "doesn't match any Serverless Functions
# inside the `api` directory".
# Patterns are gitignore syntax: anchor them to the repo root, or they also match the
# same name anywhere under src/ -- an unanchored `skills/` stripped
# src/hubspot_mcp/skills/ from the bundle and took the hosted server down.
/tests/
/docs/
/scripts/
/.github/
/reference/
/skills/
/hooks/
/bin/
/.claude/
/.claude-plugin/
